(
 'AWS vs Azure vs Google Cloud: Which Should You Learn First in 2026?',
 'aws-vs-azure-vs-google-cloud-which-to-learn-first',
 'A practical comparison of AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud for beginners — hiring demand, learning curve, certification ladders and how to pick one and commit.',
 E'If you are starting cloud engineering, the first real decision is which platform to learn. The honest answer: **the core concepts transfer**, so the platform matters less than finishing one properly. But the market you are hiring into should still guide the choice.\n\n## The short answer\n\n- **Microsoft Azure** — strongest fit if you are targeting banks, insurance, telcos, government contractors and other enterprises already running Microsoft 365 and Active Directory. Its certification ladder (AZ-900 → AZ-104 → AZ-305) is the clearest of the three.\n- **AWS** — the broadest job market overall, especially in startups, fintech and product companies. Deepest service catalogue, largest community, most tutorials.\n- **Google Cloud** — smaller share of job postings, but strong in data, analytics and machine-learning-heavy teams.\n\n## How to actually choose\n\n1. **Search live job listings in your city and target market.** Count how many mention Azure, AWS or GCP. Learn what people are hiring for, not what is trending online.\n2. **Check your existing background.** Windows/systems administration → Azure. Linux/scripting → AWS. Data analytics or Python/ML → Google Cloud.\n3. **Pick one and go deep for six months.** Employers hire depth in one platform far more readily than shallow familiarity with three.\n\n## What is the same everywhere\n\nAbout 70% of what makes a good cloud engineer is platform-neutral: Linux, networking (IP, DNS, routing, firewalls), identity and access management, infrastructure as code, containers, CI/CD, monitoring and cost control. Learn those on one platform and the second platform takes weeks, not months.\n\n## What is different\n\n| Area | AWS | Azure | Google Cloud |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Entry certification | Cloud Practitioner | AZ-900 | Cloud Digital Leader |\n| Core admin certification | Solutions Architect Associate | AZ-104 | Associate Cloud Engineer |\n| Typical employer | Startups, fintech, product teams | Enterprise, banking, public sector | Data and ML-driven teams |\n| Identity model | IAM users, roles, policies | Microsoft Entra ID, RBAC | IAM with org policies |\n\n## A six-month plan that works on any platform\n\n- **Months 1–2:** Linux command line, networking fundamentals, Git, one scripting language (Python or Bash).\n- **Month 3:** Your platform''s fundamentals certification, plus hands-on labs in the free tier.\n- **Months 4–5:** Infrastructure as code (Terraform), containers and Kubernetes, CI/CD pipelines.\n- **Month 6:** The associate-level administrator or architect certification, plus two portfolio projects deployed publicly.\n\n## Where to get help\n\nSelf-study works, but most people stall at the projects stage. Our [live, instructor-led cloud programmes](/courses) run in cohorts with real deployments, code review and interview preparation, and our [learning paths](/paths) sequence the certifications in the order employers actually ask for. If you are unsure which platform suits your background, [talk to us](/contact) before you buy anything.\n\n## Frequently asked\n\n**Can I learn two clouds at once?** You can, but you should not. Finish one associate-level track first; the second is much faster afterwards.\n\n**Do certifications alone get you hired?** No. They get you past screening. Deployed projects, a public repository and the ability to explain your architecture decisions get you the offer.\n\n**Is the free tier enough to learn?** Yes, for almost everything at beginner and associate level. Set a billing alert on day one.',
 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523474253046-8cd2748b5fd2?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80',
 'Silicon Edge Consulting', 'published', 'Cloud Engineering',
 ARRAY['aws','azure','google cloud','cloud','beginners'],
 now() - interval '5 days',
 'AWS vs Azure vs Google Cloud: Which to Learn First in 2026?',
 'AWS, Azure or Google Cloud? A beginner-focused comparison of hiring demand, certification ladders and learning curve, plus a six-month plan for the one you pick.',
 ARRAY['aws vs azure','which cloud to learn first','cloud computing course','azure training','aws training nigeria'],
