(
 'Kubernetes for Beginners: A 30-Day Learning Plan with Real Projects',
 'kubernetes-for-beginners-30-day-plan',
 'A day-by-day Kubernetes plan for engineers who already know Docker — core objects, networking, Helm, observability and three portfolio projects you can deploy.',
 E'Kubernetes is the single most requested skill in DevOps and platform engineering job adverts, and the single most abandoned learning project. The reason is usually the same: people start with cluster internals instead of the handful of objects they will use every day.\n\nThis plan assumes you can already build and run a Docker container. If you cannot yet, spend a week there first.\n\n## Week 1 — the objects you will actually use\n\n- **Days 1–2:** Install a local cluster (kind, k3d or minikube). Learn `kubectl get`, `describe`, `logs`, `exec`.\n- **Days 3–4:** Pods, ReplicaSets, Deployments. Roll out a change, then roll it back.\n- **Days 5–6:** Services and Ingress. Get traffic from your browser to a pod.\n- **Day 7:** ConfigMaps and Secrets. Move every hardcoded value out of your image.\n\n## Week 2 — running something real\n\n- **Days 8–10:** Deploy a web app plus a database using StatefulSets and PersistentVolumeClaims.\n- **Days 11–12:** Resource requests and limits, liveness and readiness probes. Break them on purpose and read what the events say.\n- **Days 13–14:** Namespaces, RBAC and service accounts. Give a workload the least privilege it can run with.\n\n**Project 1:** a three-tier application (frontend, API, database) running in one namespace with ingress and health checks.\n\n## Week 3 — packaging and automation\n\n- **Days 15–17:** Helm. Convert your YAML into a chart with values for dev and prod.\n- **Days 18–19:** Horizontal Pod Autoscaler, and a load test that proves it scales.\n- **Days 20–21:** CI/CD — build an image, push it, and deploy to the cluster from a pipeline.\n\n**Project 2:** a Helm chart plus a pipeline that deploys on every merge to main.\n\n## Week 4 — production concerns\n\n- **Days 22–24:** Observability — metrics, logs and dashboards. Answer "is it healthy?" without `kubectl`.\n- **Days 25–26:** Managed Kubernetes on a cloud provider (EKS, AKS or GKE). Note what changes: node pools, load balancers, cloud IAM.\n- **Days 27–28:** Cost and right-sizing. Find the workload wasting the most memory.\n- **Days 29–30:** Write it up. A README with an architecture diagram is worth more in interviews than another tutorial.\n\n**Project 3:** the same application on managed Kubernetes with monitoring and an incident write-up.\n\n## Common beginner mistakes\n\n- Learning etcd and control-plane internals before Deployments. Interesting, not employable yet.\n- Skipping probes and resource limits — the two things that cause most real outages.\n- Never deleting a pod to watch it self-heal. Break things deliberately in a local cluster.\n\n## Going further\n\nOur [DevOps and Kubernetes programmes](/courses) run this material live with an instructor reviewing your manifests, plus assignments graded against production practice. See the [full learning paths](/paths) if you want the container track sequenced with CI/CD and infrastructure as code.\n\n## Frequently asked\n\n**Do I need Kubernetes to get a DevOps job?** For most mid-level roles, yes — or at least a credible working knowledge of it.\n\n**Local cluster or cloud?** Learn locally (free, fast), then spend the final week on a managed cluster so you understand cloud networking and IAM integration.\n\n**Should I take the CKA?** It is a strong signal because it is hands-on. Take it after you have completed the projects above, not before.',
 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1667372393119-3d4c48d07fc9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80',
 'Silicon Edge Consulting', 'published', 'DevOps',
 ARRAY['kubernetes','devops','containers','roadmap'],
 now() - interval '3 days',
 'Kubernetes for Beginners: 30-Day Learning Plan + Projects',
 'A 30-day Kubernetes plan for engineers who know Docker: deployments, ingress, Helm, autoscaling, observability and three portfolio projects to deploy.',
 ARRAY['kubernetes for beginners','learn kubernetes','devops bootcamp','kubernetes course','cka preparation'],
