(
 'AZ-104 Study Guide: Pass the Microsoft Azure Administrator Exam in 8 Weeks',
 'az-104-study-guide-8-weeks',
 'An eight-week AZ-104 study plan mapped to the exam skills outline, with lab ideas for identity, storage, networking, compute and monitoring.',
 E'AZ-104 (Microsoft Azure Administrator) is the certification that turns "I have heard of Azure" into "I can run Azure". It is also where most self-studiers stall, because it is a hands-on exam wrapped in a large syllabus.\n\nThis plan spreads Microsoft''s published skills outline across eight weeks, with a lab for every domain. Always confirm the current exam objectives on Microsoft Learn before you book — Microsoft revises them periodically.\n\n## Before you start\n\n- Finish **AZ-900** first if cloud concepts are new. It costs little and removes half the vocabulary problems. See our [Azure certification path guide](/blog/azure-certification-path-az900-to-az104).\n- Create a free Azure account and set a **budget alert** immediately.\n- Install the Azure CLI and PowerShell Az module. The exam expects portal, CLI and template familiarity.\n\n## Week 1–2 — Identity and governance\n\nMicrosoft Entra ID users, groups, administrative units. Role-based access control and custom roles. Subscriptions, management groups, Azure Policy, resource locks and tags.\n\n**Lab:** build a two-subscription structure with a policy that blocks untagged resource creation, and a custom role that can restart VMs but not delete them.\n\n## Week 3 — Storage\n\nStorage accounts, redundancy options, blob tiers and lifecycle rules, Azure Files, shared access signatures, and storage networking rules.\n\n**Lab:** host a static site from blob storage, lock it to a virtual network, and add a lifecycle rule that moves old blobs to cool storage.\n\n## Week 4–5 — Compute\n\nVirtual machines, availability sets and zones, scale sets, disks and images. App Service plans. Azure Container Instances and Azure Kubernetes Service basics. ARM and Bicep templates.\n\n**Lab:** deploy a scale set behind a load balancer from a Bicep template, then scale it on CPU.\n\n## Week 6 — Networking\n\nVirtual networks and subnets, network security groups, peering, VPN and ExpressRoute concepts, Azure DNS, load balancer versus Application Gateway, and Network Watcher for troubleshooting.\n\n**Lab:** connect two virtual networks with peering, restrict traffic with NSGs, and prove the path with Network Watcher.\n\n## Week 7 — Monitoring and backup\n\nAzure Monitor, log analytics workspaces, alerts and action groups, Recovery Services vaults, VM backup and restore, and Azure Site Recovery basics.\n\n**Lab:** back up a VM, restore a single file, and raise an alert when CPU stays above 80% for ten minutes.\n\n## Week 8 — Exam readiness\n\nTimed practice questions, revisit weak domains, and redo the two labs you found hardest without notes. Book the exam before this week starts — a date makes you finish.\n\n## Exam-day advice\n\n- Read case-study questions from the requirements backwards. The constraint usually eliminates two answers.\n- If you can do it in the portal but cannot name the CLI command, you are half prepared. Practise both.\n- Flag and move on. Time pressure fails more candidates than knowledge gaps.\n\n## Studying with support\n\nOur [live Azure programmes](/courses) cover this syllabus in instructor-led cohorts with graded labs, and our [one-month Azure cloud engineering bootcamp](/courses) adds interview preparation on top. Compare options on the [pricing page](/pricing) or [ask us which fits your level](/contact).\n\n## Frequently asked\n\n**Is AZ-104 hard?** It is moderate — the difficulty is breadth and hands-on tasks, not depth. Consistent lab time beats reading.\n\n**How long does it take?** Eight to twelve weeks at around eight hours per week for someone with basic IT experience.\n\n**What comes after AZ-104?** AZ-305 (Solutions Architect) for design work, AZ-400 for DevOps, or AZ-500 for security.',
 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80',
 'Silicon Edge Consulting', 'published', 'Cloud Engineering',
 ARRAY['azure','az-104','certification','study plan'],
